  "result": "I fixed it in `src/lib/csv.ts:10`. I haven't run the test suite.\n\nThe CSV writer checked each field for commas and line breaks to decide whether to put it in quotes, but it didn't check for double quotes. So a title like `say \"hi\"` went out unquoted. A spreadsheet treats a bare `\"` in a field as the start or end of a quoted section, which is why the columns shifted. Titles with commas already got quoted, so they were fine.\n\nThe fix adds `\"` to that check. Fields containing a double quote are now wrapped in quotes, and the existing code doubles any quotes inside them, as the CSV standard requires. The same writer handles the activity export, so it gets the fix too.\n\n`tests/lib/csv.test.ts` already had a test for this exact case (`say \"hi\"` → `\"say \"\"hi\"\"\"`). It would have been failing before this change.",
